APPLICATION CHECKLIST

1. Check source revisions, licenses and backups; stop any build using the target tree.
2. Run git apply --check, then git apply in each specified target repository, in the
   listed order; patch paths are relative to that repository, not the Android root.
3. Review the resulting source changes and build through the ROM's normal
   device-specific workflow. Do not mix different patch editions.
4. Validate the shown codec, the selection menu and the read-back after a change
   with the receivers you actually use.
